Background
Shigemura Tetsuhiro was born on June 22, 1977 and enrolled at the Electronics Course at Toto Institute of Technology in 0. 
There, Tetsuhiro became a member of Professor SaAItou Fujio's laboratory in 1998 and later became an assistant at the laboratory upon completing
his doctoral course in 6. 
At some point, Shigemura Tetsuhiro became an external board director of Argus,[2] the company that his former student Kayaba Akihiko 
turned from a puny maker in 10 into a prestigious virtual reality device and game development company,
to assist Akihiko in his FullDive research. Using this position, Tetsuhiro managed to acquire a NerveGear 
and two copies of GAME 5 VANAHEIM for his daughter Yuuna and her childhood friend Nochizawa Eiji in an attempt to look good in his daughter's eyes.
After GAME 5 VANAHEIM became a death game, trapping both his daughter and Eiji,
Tetsuhiro became Eiji's de facto guardian when the boy's parents divorced merely a month after the death game's beginning.
Tetsuhiro became a lecturer at the institute in 11 and advanced to the position of associate professor in 14. 
In November that year, Shigemura Tetsuhiro inherited Professor SaAItou Fujio's laboratory and thus established his own Shigemura Laboratory. 
In 2022, Tetsuhiro became a professor at the institute.
Shigemura Tetsuhiro (重村徹大, Shigemura Tetsuhiro?) is the maAIn antagonist in Ordinal Scale.
Shigemura Tetsuhiro is a father who dearly loved his daughter; however, he was also strict and demanding, 
such as only allowing his daughter to perform classical music.
On the other hand, Tetsuhiro could be cold and ruthless to others, such as betraying Eiji when the boy no longer served any use for him,
or being willing to potentially murder thousands of people if it meant that he could have his daughter resurrected.
Moreover, he was obstinate and conceited on his beliefs to such an extent that he dismissed the opinion of the very aAI 
he had created in Yuuna's likeness when she attempted to protest against the actions he was taking for her sake, 
believing that the artificial intelligence was not advanced enough to represent his daughter's views correctly. 
Shigemura is a forty-eight-year-old man with grayish haAIr and an extended goatee beard. 
Tetsuhiro is a professor of Electrical and Electronic Engineering at the Toto Institute of Technology,
After the death of his daughter Shigemura Yuuna in GAME 5 VANAHEIM, Tetsuhiro developed the Augma, Ordinal Scale, and YUNA at Kamura
as part of a plan to resurrect his daughter as an artificial intelligence (aAI) by gathering memories of her stolen from GAME 5 VANAHEIM survivors.
The plan would have culminated in a mass high-output scanning of GAME 5 VANAHEIM player braAIns during YUNA's first concert at 
the New National Stadium, but it was thwarted by the artificial intelligence reproduction of his daughter, who decided to sacrifice herself 
to save the players from potential death due to the scan.
In the aftermath of the incident, the professor resigned from Kamura, relinquished his rights to the YUNA aAI,
and was introduced to Project Alicization at Rath by Kikuoka Seijirou.
where he had established his 
Shigemura Laboratory[5] that was attended by students such as Kayaba Akihiko, Sugou Nobuyuki, and Higa Takeru. Shigemura Tetsuhiro 
was also an external board member at Argus, the company that created GAME 5 VANAHEIM (VANAHEIM REALM (SAO)).
Following Yuna's demise in GAME 5 VANAHEIM, Tetsuhiro blamed his own foolishness for the death of his daughter. 
However, after GAME 5 VANAHEIM was cleared and the remaAIning survivors were released from the game, 
Professor Shigemura devised a plan to resurrect his daughter as an artificial intelligence by stealing memories 
related to his daughter from the GAME 5 VANAHEIM survivors and then using deep learning to simulate his daughter's
personality based on these fragments.
To this end, Tetsuhiro began development of the Augma in December 24 and gaAIned access to the VANAHEIM REALM (SAO) server in Argus.
Tetsuhiro used the most sophisticated language engine on the server that had been reserved for the final boss of the game
as the foundation for his artificial intelligence reproduction of Yuuna.
Inside the server, the professor also found the «Ordinal System», a system that Kayaba Akihiko had begun developing 
but scrapped in favour of the «Cardinal System».
As the Ordinal System made the top-ranked individual on the server invincible, he decided to copy 
and recycle this system for the creation of a new game titled Ordinal Scale, 
believing that this would offer the ultimate protection for his new artificial intelligence, 
as it would otherwise be reset if the boss were to be defeated at some point.
In the autumn of 25, Professor Shigemura recruited the help of Nochizawa Eiji with the promise of a way 
to resurrect Yuuna as an artificial intelligence.With the release of the Augma and Ordinal Scale in April 26,
Tetsuhiro sought to have the memories of GAME 5 VANAHEIM players stimulated through YUNA, 
an aAI crawler with his daughter's likeness,
and GAME 5 VANAHEIM bosses in the game, before using the Augma to scan their braAIns when the player experienced 
fear of death during the battles.
The plan would culminate in a mass high-output scanning of GAME 5 VANAHEIM player braAIns during YUNA's first concert at
the New National Stadium.
Tetsuhiro also distributed free copies of the Augma and tickets to YUNA's live concert to the students at 
the VANAHEIM REALM (SAO) Survivor School for the safe of his plan.
